  "question": {
    "text": "The coordinates of the points on the line&nbsp;<math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> which are equidistant from the lines <math><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> can be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>73</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>28</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>73</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>28</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>77</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>77</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that the bisectors of the angles between two lines contain all those points which are equidistant from the lines.</p><p>So, the required point lies on the bisectors of the angles between the given lines.<br />The equations of the bisectors are given by<br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><msup><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>39</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Let,&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> be the coordinates of the required point. Then,<br /><math><mn>8</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> &hellip;(i)<br />or, <math><mn>8</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>39</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> &hellip;(ii)<br />It is given that <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Therefore,<br /><math><mn>3</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> &hellip;(iii)<br />Solving (iii) with (i) and (ii) respectively, we obtain the coordinates of the required points as<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>73</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>28</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>77</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
